WEBVTT

00:00.081 --> 00:02.082
THE OUTSKIRTS URBUS RIGARDEN
SLUMLAND STREET

00:02.082 --> 00:04.082
GINA'S TAVERN
HEN AND BEANSTALK PAVILION

00:04.082 --> 00:07.007
DONNAN
Everyone got the drink?

00:07.054 --> 00:12.058
To celebrate the victory of Will,
who fought for us...

00:12.058 --> 00:15.033
Cheers!

00:16.029 --> 00:18.054
Thanks, Will!

00:19.029 --> 00:21.042
You worked hard too.

00:21.042 --> 00:23.009
Well done.

00:23.054 --> 00:26.038
Thank you for all you've done for Will.

00:28.001 --> 00:29.047
Why only to him?

00:29.047 --> 00:32.097
Prof, we didn't do anything.

00:35.064 --> 00:38.068
Please keep looking after him.

00:47.043 --> 00:48.006
So?

00:49.009 --> 00:52.037
Did you get scouted by the Tower?

00:54.062 --> 00:56.045
Of course, he didn't.

00:56.045 --> 01:00.037
Not only did we have a falling out,
we didn't even win the event.

01:01.075 --> 01:05.032
It's all Sion's fault!

01:07.023 --> 01:10.026
And where's this other teammate?

01:10.066 --> 01:12.043
I did invite him, but...

01:12.043 --> 01:14.064
Why would I go to your party?

01:14.064 --> 01:15.076
That's what he said.

01:15.076 --> 01:17.077
It's fine, isn't it?

01:17.077 --> 01:22.002
You won the fight
and we got a proper apology.

01:23.006 --> 01:24.027
Moreover...

01:24.027 --> 01:26.036
Why?!

01:26.036 --> 01:29.011
Why do I have to work
in a Dwarf's tavern?

01:29.011 --> 01:32.099
Action speaks louder than words,
for the Dwarves.

01:33.049 --> 01:36.066
It just so happens that
we're short on employees.

01:37.049 --> 01:39.087
How long are you going to take
to wash those dishes?

01:39.087 --> 01:42.008
The goulard bean sauté is ready!

01:42.008 --> 01:43.037
Yes, Ma'am!

01:43.088 --> 01:48.038
Now I won't get scouted because
I lost to that no-talent.

01:50.009 --> 01:53.031
- Damn it!
- Make sure you do it right, Boy!

01:54.026 --> 01:56.001
He got his karma.

01:56.001 --> 01:57.068
Good grief.

01:58.077 --> 02:03.001
Professor Workner,
was having a party bad idea after all?

02:03.001 --> 02:06.065
I didn't stop you all in the beginning,
so I'm not going to stop you now.

02:06.065 --> 02:11.099
Rather, after Will entered the festival
and showed all of that,

02:11.099 --> 02:14.053
how is he going to deal
with tomorrow onwards?

02:17.016 --> 02:21.045
Won't everyone see him in a new light now
that they know what he's capable of?

02:21.045 --> 02:23.079
I wonder if it's that simple.

02:25.067 --> 02:27.067
Don't say I didn't warn you.

03:52.013 --> 03:55.038
EPISODE 8: SHALL WE DATE?

04:02.026 --> 04:05.002
Almost time for the All-Student Praxis.

04:05.002 --> 04:07.077
A whole week of dungeon diving...

04:08.003 --> 04:09.044
You got your party yet?

04:09.044 --> 04:11.027
Not yet.

04:11.084 --> 04:14.098
If only I could be in a party
with this year's top three.

04:16.036 --> 04:18.003
Hey, Flunkee!

04:19.096 --> 04:22.033
Won't you go to the dungeon with us?

04:28.038 --> 04:30.005
6TH-YEAR STUDENT OF THE RIGARDEN MAGICAL ACADEMY
We admit it, you have ridiculous strength.

04:30.005 --> 04:31.096
FLIP MALTEAU - PALM SNOCK
We admit it, you have ridiculous strength.

04:32.004 --> 04:35.021
So go to the dungeon with us.

04:35.021 --> 04:37.047
We won't let you steal the start.

04:37.047 --> 04:41.022
We were already planning on
asking him to join us.

04:41.022 --> 04:43.035
Stay out of this, Emma!

04:43.035 --> 04:45.072
We saw your fight at the Magic Festival.

04:45.072 --> 04:47.085
Wanna join our party?

04:47.085 --> 04:51.002
Hang on!
Don't just jump in on your own!

04:51.002 --> 04:53.015
Come and join us.

04:53.015 --> 04:53.086
Huh?

04:53.086 --> 04:56.011
Wait... What?

05:01.049 --> 05:03.074
6TH-YEAR STUDENT OF THE RIGARDEN MAGICAL ACADEMY
WIGNALL LINDOR

05:03.074 --> 05:05.099
6TH-YEAR STUDENT OF THE RIGARDEN MAGICAL ACADEMY
SION ULSTER

05:05.099 --> 05:08.005
6TH-YEAR STUDENT OF THE RIGARDEN MAGICAL ACADEMY
LIHANNA OWENZAUS

05:10.096 --> 05:16.021
They're interested in Will after
they've seen what he can do.

05:18.009 --> 05:21.013
Is this what Professor Workner meant?

05:23.076 --> 05:25.001
Hold on a sec!

05:25.068 --> 05:30.027
You guys are so shameless,
after bullying him all this time!

05:31.099 --> 05:34.027
See, he's angry too.

05:35.015 --> 05:36.032
Colette...

05:37.019 --> 05:40.082
It's amazing!
I can't believe I got invited!

05:40.082 --> 05:43.079
Does this mean
they consider me a friend?

05:43.079 --> 05:44.078
He's a lost cause now.

05:44.078 --> 05:47.041
He's been starved for friends
for too long.

05:47.087 --> 05:49.083
Stay out of this, Colette!

05:49.083 --> 05:53.005
To begin with, you've been trying to
keep him for yourself, aren't you?

05:54.067 --> 05:56.067
Let's go to the dungeon together.

05:56.067 --> 05:59.003
Of course,
we'll split the monsters and credits.

05:59.092 --> 06:01.067
So why not come with us—

06:01.067 --> 06:02.068
No!

06:03.038 --> 06:06.035
Will has plans with me tomorrow.

06:06.035 --> 06:09.002
We'll go shopping together.

06:13.089 --> 06:17.019
I got carried away.
What have I done?

06:17.019 --> 06:19.082
It sounds like we're going on a da—

06:19.082 --> 06:22.028
I hear you're going on a date tomorrow.

06:22.028 --> 06:23.095
It's not a date, Rose!

06:23.095 --> 06:25.036
6TH-YEAR STUDENT OF THE RIGARDEN MAGICAL ACADEMY
It's not a date, Rose!

06:25.036 --> 06:27.045
ROSE PREHNITE
If you say so.

06:28.000 --> 06:29.091
Careful, it's hot.

06:29.091 --> 06:30.095
Thanks.

06:31.049 --> 06:34.004
But you'll go shopping with him, right?

06:34.004 --> 06:36.096
You should at least prepare for it,
don't you think?

06:37.038 --> 06:39.000
You're right.

06:39.000 --> 06:42.021
I have to, or it'll be rude to Will.

06:42.065 --> 06:43.072
That's it.

06:43.072 --> 06:47.072
If you wear something cute,
even a lie becomes a truth.

06:53.093 --> 06:57.004
There are no classes tomorrow.
Are you going to the dungeon again?

06:58.081 --> 07:01.065
I'm going shopping tomorrow.

07:01.065 --> 07:02.065
Shopping?

07:03.074 --> 07:06.066
It felt like I was half persuaded to go.

07:07.062 --> 07:09.007
All-Student Praxis is coming up, right?

07:09.007 --> 07:12.066
We'll need to get equipment and items.

07:12.066 --> 07:15.067
She's right.
I do need to go shopping.

07:17.067 --> 07:19.079
Is it just going to be the two of you?

07:19.079 --> 07:21.000
Yeah, what of it?

07:21.073 --> 07:23.067
Is this person Colette?

07:23.067 --> 07:25.008
I'm surprised that you know.

07:25.008 --> 07:28.043
I guess you've met her
a few times before.

07:35.031 --> 07:37.014
URBUS RIGARDEN
ST. VIOLA PLAZA

07:45.019 --> 07:48.007
Is this a date after all?

07:48.007 --> 07:52.028
Even if it isn't, it's a date.

07:52.028 --> 07:54.062
I'll make it a date.

07:59.000 --> 08:00.054
Good morning, Colette.

08:04.003 --> 08:05.088
Good morning.

08:06.003 --> 08:10.005
I had intended to come early,
but you got here earlier than me.

08:10.005 --> 08:13.014
Yeah, I just happened to
wake up early today.

08:17.048 --> 08:19.027
What is it?

08:21.019 --> 08:23.086
That dress and hairstyle
look good on you.

08:23.086 --> 08:25.009
You appear different from usual.

08:25.009 --> 08:27.061
You've made my heart race somehow.

08:34.087 --> 08:36.041
Thank you.

08:36.041 --> 08:38.000
Hey!

08:41.021 --> 08:44.013
Sorry, I'm late.
I had to take care of a few things.

08:44.013 --> 08:46.067
Morning, Will. And you, Colette.

08:50.042 --> 08:51.093
Are you...

08:52.097 --> 08:56.014
I'm Rosty Nowman, Will's roommate.

08:56.014 --> 08:59.069
I guess I've never properly
introduced myself.

08:59.069 --> 09:02.044
I'm looking forward to today, Colette.

09:03.006 --> 09:04.077
What does that mean?

09:04.077 --> 09:08.044
Rosty said he wanted to come along
no matter what.

09:08.044 --> 09:12.002
If we're going shopping,
the more the merrier.

09:14.041 --> 09:16.045
Rather than that...

09:16.097 --> 09:18.008
Let's go!

09:19.022 --> 09:21.017
There's a lot of stuff to buy, right?

09:21.017 --> 09:23.033
Don't push me, Rosty.

09:26.084 --> 09:31.038
They're just friends, aren't they?
But what's with that hand-holding?

09:40.068 --> 09:43.094
What's going on here?!

09:48.086 --> 09:50.032
Will, this is...

09:50.032 --> 09:52.095
Is this what you're looking for?

09:53.074 --> 09:55.074
Yeah, thanks.

09:57.087 --> 09:59.087
It's crooked here.

10:09.063 --> 10:13.068
Will!

10:19.063 --> 10:21.023
Colette?

10:21.023 --> 10:22.039
What's wrong?

10:23.077 --> 10:25.015
Rosty...

10:25.015 --> 10:25.081
Huh?

10:25.081 --> 10:27.077
What's with that person?!

10:27.077 --> 10:29.009
He never leaves your side!

10:29.009 --> 10:32.036
And the closeness between
the two of you is so weird!

10:32.036 --> 10:34.066
Is he really just a roommate?

10:34.066 --> 10:36.066
He has such a beautiful face.

10:36.066 --> 10:39.025
Don't tell me that he is actually a she?!

10:39.095 --> 10:42.033
What are you talking about, Colette?

10:42.033 --> 10:46.017
Rosty is a boy just like me.
There's no doubt about that.

10:46.057 --> 10:49.075
He has the thing,
and it's bigger than mine.

10:49.075 --> 10:52.034
Bigger than... Huh?!

10:53.008 --> 10:57.005
Sure, he is pretty handsy.

10:57.005 --> 10:59.093
But he's been like that
since the day we met.

11:02.027 --> 11:03.085
Even so...

11:03.085 --> 11:04.052
Here.

11:05.044 --> 11:07.028
I got some drinks.

11:08.048 --> 11:09.044
Thanks.

11:11.028 --> 11:13.057
Huh? Where's yours?

11:13.057 --> 11:14.082
I'm all right.

11:15.023 --> 11:16.095
I'll just have some of yours.

11:19.007 --> 11:21.045
I'll share mine with you.

11:25.079 --> 11:28.085
Will, you need to get
your sword maintained, right?

11:29.057 --> 11:30.084
Go ahead without us.

11:30.084 --> 11:32.046
What? But...

11:32.093 --> 11:38.005
The Dwarves won't be happy
if mages like us show up at their forge.

11:38.005 --> 11:39.097
So, go ahead.

11:41.031 --> 11:43.031
Got it.

11:44.001 --> 11:45.081
Then, I'll see you later.

11:46.048 --> 11:47.069
Later.

12:06.075 --> 12:09.012
I'm going to ask you bluntly.

12:09.012 --> 12:12.008
Am I imagining it, or do you think of Will
as more than just a friend?

12:21.089 --> 12:23.064
You're not imagining it.

12:23.064 --> 12:26.068
I love Will more than anyone.

12:26.068 --> 12:27.006
Huh?!

12:27.006 --> 12:32.073
In fact, I love him,
even more than you do.

12:34.073 --> 12:39.091
Listen, Will and I used to hug each other
all the time until four years ago!

12:39.091 --> 12:41.062
It's my dark past, though.

12:41.062 --> 12:43.008
I'm aware of that.

12:43.008 --> 12:47.002
But you've never taken a bath
with him, right?

12:47.002 --> 12:52.058
Well, not yet, but when we were
hugging each other, it was so great.

12:52.058 --> 12:56.021
We still take a bath together
every night.

12:56.065 --> 13:00.051
What do you mean by
taking a bath together?

13:00.051 --> 13:04.047
I'll leave it
to your imagination, Colette.

13:12.004 --> 13:14.098
They were both acting kind of odd.

13:15.004 --> 13:17.023
Do they not like each other?

13:19.009 --> 13:21.053
Will Serfort.

13:23.047 --> 13:24.074
Aren't you...

13:24.074 --> 13:26.024
Lihanna!

13:27.012 --> 13:29.012
Lihanna Owenzaus.

13:29.012 --> 13:34.054
The Miss Perfect, who earned all the credits
in spellwork, writing, and praxis.

13:34.054 --> 13:37.076
A person who stands high above the masses,
the exact opposite of mine.

13:38.038 --> 13:40.001
Do you need something?

13:40.092 --> 13:44.076
Do you have a moment?
It shouldn't take long.

13:45.022 --> 13:46.068
Follow me.

13:50.077 --> 13:53.027
URBUS RIGARDEN
COFFEEHOUSE "NIGHT"

14:04.007 --> 14:06.053
The final term of our last year
in the Academy...

14:06.053 --> 14:10.008
Which means it's time
for the All-Student Praxis.

14:10.054 --> 14:13.008
I want to form a party
with five of us.

14:14.072 --> 14:16.025
For a dungeon dive.

14:30.064 --> 14:34.019
What are you doing here, Flunkee?

14:34.019 --> 14:36.094
Lihanna, what's the meaning of this?

14:36.094 --> 14:40.007
Are you telling me to freeze him?

14:41.024 --> 14:44.057
Without a doubt,
two people who hate me the most.

14:44.099 --> 14:48.058
Why would you bring me here, Lihanna?

14:49.074 --> 14:51.002
Is that a no?

14:51.002 --> 14:52.083
She's an airhead!

14:52.083 --> 14:54.046
Was she this kind of girl?

14:54.046 --> 14:55.046
Hey!

14:55.046 --> 14:57.021
Don't ignore me!

15:00.025 --> 15:01.034
Fleuria.

15:06.097 --> 15:11.097
Since when have mages become
as barbaric as the Dwarves?

15:14.063 --> 15:16.006
Illusion magic.

15:16.006 --> 15:20.098
A unique type of magic that summons fantasy
landscapes granted only to the Elves.

15:20.098 --> 15:24.049
Let's hear Lihanna out first, shall we?

15:26.066 --> 15:29.024
It's as I explained in the beginning.

15:29.024 --> 15:32.004
All-Student Praxis is about to begin.

15:32.004 --> 15:34.075
I want to form a party of
the best mages in our year,

15:34.075 --> 15:39.000
together with the person who stood out
the most at the festival.

15:39.042 --> 15:42.009
He has something that we're lacking.

15:42.009 --> 15:44.084
And that will help us in the dungeon.

15:45.042 --> 15:47.038
That's how I judged it.

15:47.038 --> 15:50.064
I doubt that judgment of yours, Lihanna.

15:51.005 --> 15:55.048
Bringing someone who can't use Search
will only slow us down.

15:55.048 --> 15:59.002
I think you're being misled by
a curiosity through his small feat.

15:59.002 --> 16:03.003
I don't want to be in a party
with him again either.

16:04.053 --> 16:07.045
Meaningless pride and animosity.

16:07.045 --> 16:11.078
Sounds to me like you two are
just bitter about losing to him.

16:12.024 --> 16:16.000
I wonder why you are able to look down
on someone who defeated you two.

16:16.000 --> 16:17.066
I question your character.

16:17.066 --> 16:19.004
What did you say?

16:19.004 --> 16:23.075
He has brute strength of Dwarves
and monster-like agility.

16:23.075 --> 16:26.017
Though there's not an ounce
of sophistication in it,

16:26.017 --> 16:29.043
his sword defeated your wands.

16:29.043 --> 16:30.084
That's all that matters.

16:31.043 --> 16:37.056
Aren't you still behind
Lihanna in credits, O noble elf?

16:37.056 --> 16:39.002
Indeed I am.

16:39.002 --> 16:42.031
Which is why I respect her opinion.

16:42.031 --> 16:48.007
If she sees something in him,
then I'll respect the no-talent, too.

16:48.049 --> 16:50.032
Unlike the two of you.

16:53.083 --> 16:59.004
I want to use all of you to go up
the Tower as the top student.

16:59.046 --> 17:04.096
I want more fame and honor,
as well as a better future for myself.

17:04.096 --> 17:08.009
Did you not get scouted
at the festival?

17:08.009 --> 17:10.097
The Thunder Faction
did reach out to me.

17:11.039 --> 17:14.003
You have a guaranteed
post-graduation placement.

17:14.003 --> 17:15.047
Why go to all this trouble?

17:18.001 --> 17:21.006
Because we, who are still in the Academy,
are the leftovers.

17:22.001 --> 17:24.011
In other words, the inferiors.

17:24.057 --> 17:26.011
Inferior?

17:27.086 --> 17:30.049
I am from House Owenzaus.

17:30.049 --> 17:32.095
The members of our family
generally die young.

17:32.095 --> 17:38.002
To prevent our ruin,
I need to deliver overwhelming results.

17:39.058 --> 17:42.029
Simply ascending the Tower
won't be enough.

17:42.029 --> 17:46.063
When it comes to it,
I have to become a Magia Vander.

17:48.042 --> 17:52.009
Surely I can't be the only one
with ambitions here.

17:54.005 --> 17:56.006
If you deem my proposal
to be of benefit to you,

17:56.093 --> 18:00.052
drop the coin in front of you
and place it in the goblet.

18:03.044 --> 18:05.061
I agree.

18:05.061 --> 18:09.061
There will be no party capable of
achieving better results than this.

18:09.061 --> 18:14.011
I pretty much have no other choice
if I want more credits, do I?

18:22.005 --> 18:23.062
And I...

18:31.009 --> 18:32.009
Will!

18:33.026 --> 18:34.089
Where were you?

18:34.089 --> 18:37.076
You weren't at the forge.

18:37.076 --> 18:39.001
So we went looking for you.

18:40.052 --> 18:41.039
Will?

18:42.048 --> 18:44.048
Colette. Rosty.

18:55.003 --> 18:57.003
About the All-Student Praxis...

18:57.003 --> 18:59.012
I'll be joining Lihanna's party.

19:13.034 --> 19:17.093
As you all know, the All-Student Praxis
will begin in ten days.

19:19.003 --> 19:23.006
Floors that were off limits,
seven through ten, will be unlocked.

19:23.006 --> 19:29.027
Enabling you to fight Over-Five Enemies
and other high-credit monsters.

19:29.027 --> 19:34.009
All-Student Praxis will be the only opportunity
to earn more than 1,000 credits at once.

19:35.034 --> 19:37.075
Especially Floor Keepers,
if you defeat any of them,

19:37.075 --> 19:40.033
you'll earn a large number of credits.

19:40.033 --> 19:44.022
Whether you're looking to make up for
a shortfall in credits or achievements,

19:44.022 --> 19:46.042
or hoping to ascend the Tower,
this is your chance.

19:46.087 --> 19:51.038
In theory, you can earn full Praxis credits
through the All-Student Praxis.

19:51.092 --> 19:54.017
Needless to say, some of you can die.

19:54.017 --> 19:58.026
Last year, four students
were eaten by monsters.

19:58.026 --> 20:01.081
During the Praxis, the professors
are stationed in the dungeon.

20:01.081 --> 20:04.061
But that has never stopped those
from meeting a miserable end.

20:05.048 --> 20:08.031
Recklessness is prohibited.
Forget about playing the hero.

20:08.094 --> 20:10.081
What is sought of each of you

20:10.081 --> 20:14.057
is not the aspiration to
become Magia Vander.

20:14.057 --> 20:18.002
But the steel rationality of those
who know their limits.

20:18.002 --> 20:18.077
THE DUNGEON 6TH FLOOR

20:18.077 --> 20:19.057
CONNECTING PASSAGE TO THE 7TH FLOOR,
RIGARDEN BASE CAMP

20:22.083 --> 20:26.083
Colette, I don't remember
inviting you to join us.

20:27.039 --> 20:31.004
Why not?
If Will's going, then so am I.

20:31.004 --> 20:32.034
I see.

20:33.009 --> 20:36.072
Artificier students are stationed
in the base camp.

20:36.072 --> 20:39.022
Sorry, I can't go with you.

20:39.022 --> 20:43.097
That's okay. You've prepared
a lot of magic items for me.

20:45.014 --> 20:46.035
Be careful, okay?

20:46.035 --> 20:47.045
I will.

20:49.035 --> 20:50.085
It's time.

20:50.085 --> 20:51.074
THE DUNGEON 6TH FLOOR
BASE CAMP, CENTRAL SQUARE

20:51.074 --> 20:54.009
The All-Student Praxis,
or known as the field intensive.

20:54.009 --> 20:56.049
You have one week.

20:56.049 --> 21:00.099
Unlike an ordinary Praxis,
this is a survival within the dungeon.

21:01.066 --> 21:02.066
We've set up base camps on each floor.

21:02.066 --> 21:05.024
THE DUNGEON 8TH FLOOR
We've set up base camps on each floor.

21:05.024 --> 21:06.075
Make sure to check the maps we gave.

21:06.075 --> 21:08.004
THE DUNGEON 10TH FLOOR
Make sure to check the maps we gave.

21:08.004 --> 21:09.005
THE DUNGEON 10TH FLOOR
If you choose to discontinue or retire,

21:09.005 --> 21:10.009
If you choose to discontinue or retire,

21:10.009 --> 21:12.071
make sure to get to safety.

21:12.071 --> 21:13.075
THE DUNGEON 10TH FLOOR
The professors will be standing by.

21:13.075 --> 21:14.059
The professors will be standing by.

21:18.072 --> 21:22.058
Let the All-Student Praxis begin!

23:07.041 --> 23:09.062
That bastard.

23:09.062 --> 23:13.008
"Go retrieve that thing secretly," my ass.

23:13.008 --> 23:16.058
The timing coincides
with the brats' festival.

23:24.005 --> 23:28.047
That leaves us with no choice
but to slaughter them.

